  "id": "Compound::DB08899 - Gene::5243",
  "verbalization": "Enzalutamide is implicated in the induction of Abcb1 through its inclusion in Cytochrome P450 2c9 and 2c19 inducer pathways, which are linked to Carbamazepine and Phenytoin. These inducers activate the Abcb1 gene, leading to increased expression of the transporter, which is associated with drug resistance. The mechanism is supported by the binding of Carbamazepine and Phenytoin to Abcb1, suggesting a conserved pathway involving the transporter. The low common ancestor of Enzalutamide and these inducers points to a shared regulatory mechanism, reinforcing the link between Enzalutamide and Abcb1. The evidence suggests that Enzalutamide may modulate Abcb1 expression through its role in inducing P450 enzymes, which in turn upregulate Abcb1. This relationship is biologically plausible and consistent with the observed binding of inducers to Abcb1. The mechanism is further supported by the presence of similar pathways involving other inducers, indicating a broader regulatory network.",
